Z||000003||stimpy||02-08-2001||12:40 PM||||Unfortunately, the s/c3800 is not all that pretty of an engine. That's why GM covers it with a big plastic shroud.  To the unwashed public, a clean stock 2.8 has more visual appeal.  The impressive part about them is the neck-snapping acceleration and that nifty blower whine.  I would like to see someone develop a carbon-fiber shroud for these. I'd get my dad one for his.||||reg||1
